ARENA+ demo artwork
===================

The photographs in this directory come from Wikimedia Commons and are used under the licences
below. Each was cropped to the slot it fills and re-encoded as JPEG; nothing else was changed.
Attribution is a condition of most of these licences, so this file ships with the images.

This list is written from apps/arena/public/feed.json, which is what the app draws: every
picture in it carries the same credit at runtime. Files with no entry here are generated
gradients from tools/arena-art.mjs and are covered by this repository's own licence.

What the licences do not settle
-------------------------------

A free copyright licence settles copyright and nothing else. The claims below run over parts of
this set. None of them stops the pictures being used in a demo, and none of them is met by
crediting the photographer; each is a condition on what the picture may be used for, so anyone
taking this further than a demo has to decide about them deliberately.

A PERMISSION WITH NO DEED. Nearly every licence below is a standard public licence, and the deed
linked beside it is the whole of the terms. This file is not. Its grant is the rights-holder's
own, a line in a website imprint quoted on the Commons page, which Commons accepts and the API
reads cleanly. It is the closest thing in this set to a federation press image, and the only
place its terms are written down is that page, so read the page before relying on the file:

  live-1.jpg — Football match action
  https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Attila_Szalai_in_action_for_Hungary_in_the_international_match_(October_2020).jpg

PERSONALITY RIGHTS. A photograph of an identifiable person may be taken and published, but in
much of Europe it may not be used so as to suggest that the person endorses a product or a
service, and a tile in a shipping app is a product context in a way a demo is not. Commons tags
these files. Treat the tag as a floor rather than the list: identifiable athletes appear in
roughly half this set, and Commons tags a file only when somebody has thought to.

